 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Polarity",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Pin 1 is the anode (+), pin 2 the cathode. The top face has a green corner mark at the pin 2 end; the bottom face has a green triangle whose point faces pin 2. On the carrier tape the cathode end of each part faces the sprocket holes."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Drive",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "Drive it at its rated current through a series current-limiting resistor; with no resistor a small supply change makes a large current change and can destroy it. Surges at switch-on and switch-off damage it, as does excess forward voltage or more than 5 V reverse, whether in service or under test."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current, temperature and colour",
   "page": 11,
   "text": "The white point moves a little with drive current, and each LED is meant to have its own resistor in series. Its own heating and the ambient temperature also change it: output efficiency drops and the colour shifts as it gets hotter, so the design must deal with heat."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Bins",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Use one bin per product; LEDs from different bins side by side can show a clear colour mismatch."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Handling and soldering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "The encapsulant is soft and the emitting face and plastic body are easily damaged by force, so handle the parts gently. Reflow to the profile, at most twice, with an easily washed flux, and keep the emitting face clean, since residue alters the colour. Hand soldering is only for repair and rework: a single pass at no more than 300 °C, finished in 3 s, with an iron rated 25 W or less. Do not touch the lens while hot; after soldering apply no force, shock or vibration to the lens and do not bend the board."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Cleaning and chemicals",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Ultrasonic cleaning is not allowed. Clean by wiping or dipping in isopropyl or pure alcohol, at most one minute, then let the parts stand 15 minutes at room temperature before use, and check the emitting face is clean. Thinner, trichloroethylene, acetone, sulphides, nitrides, acids, alkalis and salts all harm the LED."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Potting and adhesives",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Volatile substances can enter the package and, with light and heat in operation, discolour it and sharply reduce its output. Test the compatibility of every material used with it, mount it with adhesives that give off no organic vapour, and before using an ordinary potting compound light a small trial batch for 168 h at room temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Storage and moisture",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Unopened, store at 30 °C or below and under 60 % RH and use within a year. The part absorbs moisture: after opening, use it within 7 days at 30 °C or below and within 60 % RH, or it can crack during reflow and change colour. Bake unused parts, 60 ±5 °C for 24 h on the reel or 105 ±5 °C for 1 h loose, then reseal them in a foil bag or keep them in a nitrogen dry cabinet. Store away from acids, alkalis, corrosive gas, strong vibration and strong magnetic fields."
  },
  {
   "topic": "ESD",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "Static discharge and voltage spikes damage the LED, including the transient when the light is switched on or off. Use grounded wrist straps, gloves and shoes, and ground all equipment and instruments. A damaged LED leaks much more in reverse, has a lower forward voltage at low current, or fails to light at low current."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Packing",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "3000 pieces per reel on 8 mm embossed carrier tape, with a leader and trailer. The labelled reel is packed in an anti-static, moisture-proof aluminium foil bag."
  }
 ],
